Plan for ADXL345 accelerometer on pico

Single core for simplicity. Switch between burst sampling and processing / sending.

cycle() will produce a py dict similar to the original esp code:

Prepare sensor: write measure bit to wake from sleep, set bandwidth and range
Read from I2C devaddr 0x53 6 bytes from memaddr 0x32 
Read data into buffer as fast as possible (for a fixed number of samples, or until duration passed?)

Pre-process: assemble bytes, convert to floats, scale into m/s2
Post-process:
  Remove average / DC offset (sensor could be in any orientation)
  RMS / magnitude buffer (sum vs hypot)
  FFT buffer
  add peak frequency (highest bin) (as float)
  add acceleration (total RMS? what calculation formula? RMS of all accu samples?)

Submit over MQTT
  add id (machine) and timestamp


Take inspiration for reading sensor from:
  https://github.com/alcalyn/adxl345/blob/master/adxl345/adxl345.py
  https://github.com/pimoroni/adxl345-python/blob/master/adxl345.py
  https://github.com/adafruit/Adafruit_Python_ADXL345/blob/master/Adafruit_ADXL345/ADXL345.py

Possible FFT libraries:
  https://github.com/peterhinch/micropython-fourier
  https://github.com/v923z/micropython-ulab
